{{Nihongo|'''Takeru Fujimoto'''|藤本 健|Fujimoto Takeru; born February 24, 1977}} is a Sanese politician and former professional athlete currently serving as the [[Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology (Okaiken)|Minister of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology]] in the [[Second Honda cabinet]]. A member of the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken]], he represents the [[Kagami Prefecture|Kagami]] 2nd district in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]].

Fujimoto is widely known for his "Martial Educator" persona, combining his background in professional rugby with a rigorous approach to Sanese pedagogy.

==Early life and athletic career==
Fujimoto was born and raised in [[Aizawa]], a city known for its heavy industry and rugged coastal climate. He attended Aizawa University, where he excelled in both academics and athletics.

Before entering politics, Fujimoto was a celebrated figure in Sanese sports. He served as the captain of the '''Aizawa Eagles''', a premier team in [[Okaiken League One Rugby]], for over five seasons. Known for his "unbreakable" defensive line and disciplined leadership, he led the Eagles to a national championship more than 15 years ago. He retired from professional rugby at the peak of his career to pursue a vocation in education, citing a desire to "strengthen the spirit of the next generation."

==Educational career and media==
Following his athletic retirement, Fujimoto worked as a physical education instructor and later as a school administrator in Aizawa Prefecture. During this period, he became a household name among elementary students after providing the voice for Takeru a central character in the national [[w:English language|Trent language]] textbook series used for 3rd and 4th-grade students. His booming, authoritative, yet encouraging voice was credited with making language learning more engaging for young boys.

==Political career==
Fujimoto entered politics in 2021, successfully running for the [[Kagami Prefecture|Kagami]] 2nd district seat. He aligned himself with the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken|Progressive Party's]] "Strength and Science" wing.

===Minister of Education===
In November 2025, Prime Minister [[Honda Shigetsuma]] appointed Fujimoto as the Minister of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology. His appointment was seen as a move to appeal to the "National Vigor" sentiment rising in Okaiken.

====The "Forged-Iron" Program====
Fujimoto's signature policy is the '''"Forged-Iron" Education Program''' ({{nihongo|Rentetsu-kyōiku|錬鉄教育}}). Drawing heavily from his rugby background, the program emphasizes three core pillars:
* '''Mandatory Participation:''' Requiring students to engage in intensive group activities, whether in sports or the arts, to prevent social withdrawal.
* '''Physical and Mental Strength:''' Integrating resilience training and rigorous physical standards into the standard curriculum.
* '''Radical Teamwork:''' Grading systems that reward collective achievement over individual competition, aimed at fostering national unity.

Critics from the [[Okaiken Socialist Party|Socialist Party]] have expressed concerns regarding the program's perceived "martial" undertones, but Fujimoto has remained steadfast, famously stating, "A soft education produces a brittle nation."

==Personal life==
Fujimoto maintains a strict personal fitness regimen and is often seen practicing traditional Sanese calligraphy. He continues to be a vocal advocate for rugby at the grassroots level and frequently visits school clubs in his district to personally coach student athletes.

